    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d305">

                <pb facs="0585" n="515" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg515"/>

                <head>No. 305.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. West.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-07-26"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 26,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to Mr. Saurin’s note of the
                    28th of February last, referring to previous correspondence and denying the
                    reports received by this Government to the effect that the Milk River country
                    was overrun with Canadian Indians and half-breeds, I now have the honor to
                    inclose herewith for the information of Her Majesty’s Government a copy of a
                    letter to this Department from the War Department on the subject.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELISTGHUYSEN</signed></closer>























